diff --git a/guidance.md b/guidance.md
index a6994b1..7b9f130 100644
--- a/guidance.md
+++ b/guidance.md
@@ -1 +1,13 @@
 Use the provided spreadsheet tools to complete the requested workbook. Preserve source inputs.
+
+Before writing formulas, run `workbook_inspect` on the source: read every label, unit and comment, and note which cells are intentionally blank so they stay blank.
+
+Plan each formula from the row labels, units and comments rather than from the numeric result you expect. Formulas must reference the workbook's input cells with A1 references in the sheet that holds them, so the workbook stays live; hard-coded numbers are not acceptable answers.
+
+Write with `workbook_write` and pass `recalculate: true`. Check the tool response four ways before you stop:
+- `recalculation.recalculated` must be true; if it is false, fix the cause instead of delivering the unchecked file.
+- every formula you wrote must have a numeric value, not an engine error such as `#VALUE!`, `#REF!` or `#NAME?`;
+- `warnings`, if present, list cells whose value was stored as text rather than a formula - rewrite those as formulas;
+- sanity-check the values against the sheet's own arithmetic (ratios within range, margins consistent with revenue and profit, schedules that tie out to their opening balances).
+
+Only ever write into destination cells that the request asks for. Never overwrite source inputs, labels, year headers, units or intentional blanks. Keep the original comments in place.
